From 931de9114da406626a6abdfb188f9b761a473106 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Pray <nickwpray@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:55:02 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fork: meter bars stay crisp under zoom and follow real
 voice levels

The mini meter snaps to whole device pixels so all three bars render the
same width at any zoom or scale factor. Mic level now maps through a
shared dB scale (noise floor -55, full scale -10 dBFS) on web for both
realtime voice and dictation, so normal speech gives full motion. Silent
listening shows a travelling wave and Thinking a calm centre-out breath.
The design frame gets a realistic recorded-style volume trace.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
